From eaa654ab737c9f3238657a63cbd2b13c76cbef57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Tue, 31 Mar 2026 20:31:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] add GSI_DISP debug logging to display power and boot
 animation paths

add verbose Slog.i / ALOGI traces tagged GSI_DISP to the Java-side
display power management and native boot animation code.  covers:

PowerManagerService:
- updatePowerStateLocked: dirty flags, power group ready state
- setWakefulnessLocked: wakefulness transitions with reason and uid

DisplayManagerService:
- requestDisplayStateInternal: display id, target state, brightness

DisplayPowerController:
- updatePowerStateInternal: policy, target display state, post-animate
  actual state
- animateScreenStateChange: current/target state, color fade level,
  screen off transition flag
- setScreenState: full state with blockers, reported policy
- blockScreenOn / unblockScreenOn: timing
- screenTurningOn WM callback result

DisplayPowerState:
- setScreenState: old -> new state with reason
- setColorFadeLevel: old -> new level
- prepareColorFade / dismissColorFade / dismissColorFadeResources

ColorFade:
- prepare: mode, display dimensions, color mode, capture result,
  surface control creation
- dismiss / dismissResources
- showSurface: alpha and mode

BootAnimation (native):
- onFirstRef, readyToRun, initDisplaysAndSurfaces: lifecycle and
  display enumeration
- EGL context/surface creation and eglMakeCurrent result
- threadLoop: animation file selection (zip vs fallback logo)
- android(): mask/shine texture loading with dimensions
- movie(): entry with display count
- initTexture: per-asset load
- findBootAnimationFile: search entry

all lines use the GSI_DISP tag prefix for easy filtering:
  adb logcat | grep GSI_DISP

debug-only patch -- not for release builds.
